body:
Behavior described by this issue is what I would expect, though not what I'd like. I remember a comment during the review that said that measuring `onOpen` errors is too late because it won't catch exceptions throw when opening websocket fails. So current implementation doesn't take into consideration exceptions thrown by user in `@OnOpen` method because technically, it is an error after connection has been opened.

I spend 15 minutes looking for that comment and can't find it, maybe we could get feedback from @mkouba and @brunobat what is the behavior they expect and based on that act.

@geoand https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/pull/47415 is fine if we are going to consider these errors as well, I didn't check yet if your PR handles all the situations, but on the first look it looks good.
